 "result": "Order of calls (package is `tessel`, a Flask-style framework):\n\n1. `Tessel.__call__` — `src/tessel/app.py:1618`; just delegates.\n2. `Tessel.wsgi_entry` — `src/tessel/app.py:1566`; the real WSGI entry point.\n3. `Tessel.request_context(environ)` — `src/tessel/app.py:1501`; builds the context (and request) from the environ.\n4. `AppContext.push` — `src/tessel/ctx.py:416`; activates the context, sends `appcontext_pushed`, opens the session (`_get_session`).\n5. `AppContext.match_request` — `src/tessel/ctx.py:405`; URL routing, which stores `url_rule`/`view_args` or a `routing_exception` on the request.\n6. `Tessel.run_full_request` — `src/tessel/app.py:992`; sends `request_started`.\n7. `Tessel.preprocess_request` — `src/tessel/app.py:1366`; runs before-request handlers, and a non-`None` return short-circuits the view.\n8. `Tessel.run_view` — `src/tessel/app.py:966`:\n   - raises any routing exception (`raise_routing_exception`, line 560)\n   - handles automatic OPTIONS\n   - calls `ensure_sync(self.view_functions[rule.endpoint])(**view_args)` (line 990), which is where the view runs.\n\nAfterward `run_full_request` goes to `finalize_request` (line 1021). Exceptions from steps 7–8 go to `route_user_fault`, and exceptions that escape `run_full_request` go to `route_unhandled_fault` (line 897).",
